#250
The Lychgate in the Wood~
Black pines crowd close on every side, their needles whispering in a wind
you cannot feel. A crooked path ends at a roofed lychgate of rotting oak,
beyond which a ruined gothic cathedral rises from the fog, its spires
broken like old teeth. Lantern light glows within. Fresh graves line the
path and a rusted spade leans against the gate.
